## JSON attributes

Write `config_json` with `jsonencode()`. The provider decodes it as protobuf JSON and refuses an unknown field at plan time. It keeps your JSON in state as written; `normalized_config_json` shows what the server stored, including the routes it expands from the tree.

- Use the snake_case field names below. The camelCase protobuf JSON names also work, but import and drift write snake_case.
- Write enum values as the full names listed.
- "Required" means the server refuses the policy without the field. "Read-only" fields appear only in `normalized_config_json`; do not configure them.

### config_json

`AlertNotificationPolicyConfigV1`.

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `tree` | object | `tree` or `routes` | `{ nodes }`, a route tree of 1 to 100 nodes, described below. When `tree` has nodes, `routes` is ignored. |
| `routes` | list(object) | `tree` or `routes` | A flat list of up to 100 routes, the older form, described below. |
| `grouping` | object | Optional | How alerts are grouped into one notification. |
| `notifications` | object | Optional | Repeat and resolve behaviour. |
| `escalation` | object | Optional | Escalation steps. |
| `max_pages_per_day` | int32 | Optional | Page budget per day, 0 to 100,000. If only the weekly budget is set, this defaults to `5`. |
| `max_pages_per_week` | int32 | Optional | Page budget per week, 0 to 100,000. If only the daily budget is set, this defaults to `20`. |
| `inhibit_matching_alerts` | bool | Optional | When `true`, and the policy is enabled, notifications for every alert that matches `inhibition_matcher` are suppressed, whichever policy routes them. An empty matcher matches every alert. Defaults to `false`. |
| `inhibition_matcher` | list(object) | Optional | Matcher clauses, described below, for `inhibit_matching_alerts`. |

A tree node, `AlertPolicyTreeNodeV1`:

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `node_key` | string | Required | Unique within the tree. Route nodes become routes with this key. |
| `parent_node_key` | string | Optional | `node_key` of a branch. Omit it for a root. The tree needs at least one root, no cycles, and at most 8 levels. |
| `node_kind` | enum | Required | `ALERT_POLICY_TREE_NODE_KIND_V1_BRANCH` groups children and needs at least one. `ALERT_POLICY_TREE_NODE_KIND_V1_ROUTE` delivers and has no children. |
| `enabled` | bool | Set it | Omitted, it is stored as `false` and the node, with everything under it, never routes. Set `true`. |
| `priority` | int32 | Optional | Order among siblings, 0 to 10,000, lowest first. |
| `matcher` | list(object) | Optional | Matcher clauses. A node also requires its ancestors' clauses, and a clause that contradicts an ancestor's is refused. |
| `behavior` | enum | Route nodes | `ALERT_NOTIFICATION_ROUTE_BEHAVIOR_V1_STOP` ends evaluation after a match. `ALERT_NOTIFICATION_ROUTE_BEHAVIOR_V1_CONTINUE` goes on to later routes. A branch without it continues. |
| `target` | object | Route nodes | Exactly one of `destination_id`, `destination_key`, `group_id`, or `group_key`, naming an enabled [o11y_alert_destination](alert_destination.md) or [o11y_alert_notification_group](alert_notification_group.md). Branches have none. |
| `notification_template_id` | string | Optional | UUID of a published [o11y_alert_notification_template](alert_notification_template.md), on a route node whose target delivers by email or Slack. Omit it for the O11y.one default template. |
| `requested_notification_template_revision_id` | string | Optional | UUID of a published revision of that template, to pin it. Requires `notification_template_id`. Omit it to bind the revision published when the policy is saved. |
| `bound_notification_template_revision_id` | string | Read-only | The revision the server bound. |

A route in `routes`, `AlertNotificationRouteV1`, takes `route_key` (required and unique) and the node fields `enabled`, `priority`, `matcher`, `behavior` (required), `target` (required), `notification_template_id`, and `requested_notification_template_revision_id`. `id`, `tree_path`, and `bound_notification_template_revision_id` are read-only.

A matcher clause, `AlertMatcherClauseV1`:

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `field` | string | Required | What to match, unique within the matcher: `severity`, `class`, `detector_kind`, `mode`, `definition_id`, `dedupe_key`, `instance_key`, or an alert dimension or scope key such as `service_name`. ASCII letters, digits, `_`, `.`, `-`, and `/`, at most 128 bytes. |
| `values` | list(object) | Required | 1 to 50 values, each one of `string_value` (at most 256 bytes), `number_value`, or `bool_value`. |

An alert matches when every clause matches, and a clause matches when any of its values equals the alert's value. At most 32 clauses.

`grouping`, `AlertNotificationGroupingV1`:

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `group_by` | list(string) | Optional | Up to 8 unique fields; alerts with the same values share a notification. |
| `group_wait_seconds` | int32 | Optional | 0 to 3,600 seconds to wait before the first notification of a group. Defaults to `0`. |
| `group_interval_seconds` | int32 | Optional | 0 to 86,400 seconds between notifications for a group. Defaults to `0`. |

`notifications`, `AlertNotificationTimingV1`:

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `repeat_interval_seconds` | int32 | When `repeat_limit` is above 0 | 60 to 604,800 seconds between reminders. Ignored when `repeat_limit` is 0. |
| `repeat_limit` | int32 | Optional | 0 to 24 reminders. Defaults to `0`. |
| `notify_resolved` | bool | Optional | Send a notification when the alert resolves. Defaults to `false` when omitted. |

`escalation`, `AlertEscalationScheduleV1`:

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `schedule_key` | string | Required | Name of the schedule. |
| `steps` | list(object) | Optional | Up to 8 steps, each `{ delay_seconds, target }`. `delay_seconds` is 60 to 604,800 and strictly increasing; `target` is as for a route node. `expanded_destination_ids` is read-only. |

## Behaviour notes

- The server checks targets, templates, and published revisions when the policy is saved, and refuses a missing, disabled, or archived one.
- A template binding on a target that delivers by webhook or PagerDuty is refused: templates render only for email and Slack.

## Import

```shell
terraform import {{.Name}}.example <policy id>
```

After import `config_json` holds the server's expanded form, the same as `normalized_config_json`. The first apply writes your `config_json` back as a new policy revision.
